.TH NETWORK-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-17" "network-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
network-revamped \- network throughput in the tmux status bar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B network-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ name ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B network-revamped
shows the download and upload rates of one interface in the tmux status
line, with its LAN and public addresses, the VPN, the Wi\-Fi name and signal,
the count of connections, the latency and whether the internet is in reach.
The rate is the change in the interface's byte counters over the
milliseconds passed.
.PP
The entry point
.B network-revamped.tmux
runs
.B apply
once when tmux loads the plugin, which binds the popup key in one tmux call
and replaces the placeholders #{net_download}, #{net_upload}, #{net_speed},
#{net_fg_color}, #{net_bg_color}, #{net_vpn}, #{net_vpn_name}, #{net_ip},
#{net_wifi}, #{net_ssid}, #{net_connections}, #{net_ping}, #{net_public_ip}
and #{net_online} in status-left and status-right.
.PP
A status call prints the stored reading at once. When the rates are older
than the interval it starts one sample in the background, so the status line
never waits. A probe runs only for a placeholder the status line uses, each
at its own interval, and the three that call out stay off until their
options turn them on. Run with no command on a terminal, the tool offers a
menu.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Bind the popup key and replace the status placeholders now. In the options render mode it also starts the daemon.
.TP
.B list
Print every tmux command apply would send, one per line, and change nothing.
.TP
.B status
Print one placeholder from the stored reading: download, upload, speed, fg_color, bg_color, vpn, vpn_name, ip, wifi, ssid, connections, ping, public_ip or online. The status line runs it, and it starts a sample in the background when the stored rates are older than the interval.
.TP
.B refresh
Sample the network now, run the probes the status line uses, store the reading and say what moves.
.TP
.B card
Read everything now and print one row per reading: the interface, both rates, the addresses, the VPN, the Wi-Fi, the connections, the latency and reachability. A probe that calls out and is off is named as off.
.TP
.B popup
Open the card in a tmux popup that closes on Enter. The popup key runs it. It needs tmux 3.2 or later.
.TP
.B daemon
Sample the network and publish every placeholder the status line uses, once per interval, until another daemon takes over or the tmux server ends. apply starts it in the options render mode.
.TP
.B doctor
Print one row per dependency: tmux, each tool or file a reading comes from, how finely the clock counts, the key it found bound, gum and the core tools.
A settings row names any setting whose value it does not know.
Exits 1 only when a required tool is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, then the tmux version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
.B list
prints one JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.TP
.BI \-\- setting " value"
Any tmux option below, named with dashes, such as
.B \-\-interval
or
.BR \-\-vpn\-name\-label .
It also takes the form
.IR \-\-setting = value ,
and outranks the environment and the tmux option. Given to
.BR apply ,
it rides on the popup key and on every status call.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BI NETWORK_REVAMPED_ SETTING
Any tmux option below in capitals, such as
.BR NETWORK_REVAMPED_INTERVAL .
It outranks the tmux option.
.TP
.B NETWORK_REVAMPED_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B NETWORK_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B NETWORK_REVAMPED_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The accent of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when
.B NETWORK_REVAMPED_ACCENT
is not set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
An empty tmux option means its default. A key set to off binds nothing.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_popup_key
The prefix key that opens the detail popup. off binds nothing. The default is M\-e, left alone when someone else holds it.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_interface
The interface to measure. Empty follows the default route. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_interval
Seconds a rate sample stays fresh before the counters are read again. The default is 2.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_precision
Decimal places of a rate, 0 to 9. A rate that rounds to 1000 or more moves up a unit, through TB/s. The default is 1.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_smoothing
Weight in percent, 1 to 99, of the previous rate in a moving average. 0 shows each sample. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_render
jobs turns each placeholder into a call the status line runs. options turns it into a read of a tmux option that the daemon fills, so a status refresh starts no process. The default is jobs.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_ping_enabled
1 pings 8.8.8.8 for #{net_ping}. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_public_ip_enabled
1 asks icanhazip.com for the public address. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_online_enabled
1 requests www.gstatic.com/generate_204 with curl, or pings when curl is missing. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_vpn_interval
Seconds between VPN link probes. The default is 30.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_vpn_name_interval
Seconds between VPN name probes. The default is 30.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_ip_interval
Seconds between LAN address probes. The default is 30.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_connections_interval
Seconds between connection counts. The default is 30.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_wifi_interval
Seconds between Wi-Fi signal probes. The default is 30.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_ssid_interval
Seconds between Wi-Fi name probes. The default is 30.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_online_interval
Seconds between reachability probes. The default is 30.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_ping_interval
Seconds between pings. The default is 15.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_public_ip_interval
Seconds between public address fetches. The default is 300.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_speed_format
The printf format for download, then upload, in #{net_speed}. The default is %s %s.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_ping_format
The printf format for the latency. The default is %sms.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_wifi_format
The printf format for the Wi\-Fi signal. The default is %sdBm.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_online_up_text
What #{net_online} prints when the probe page answers. The default is on.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_online_down_text
What #{net_online} prints when it does not, shown only while the probe is on. The default is off.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_icons
nerd puts a Nerd Font glyph before every metric. ascii adds none. The default is ascii.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_fixed_width
on pads a rate and the latency on the left to their widest form, so the status line does not shift. The default is off.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_download_label
The label printed before the download rate, only when it has a value. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_upload_label
The label printed before the upload rate, only when it has a value. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_speed_label
The label printed before both rates, only when it has a value. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_vpn_label
The label printed before the VPN link, only when it has a value. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_vpn_name_label
The label printed before the VPN name, only when it has a value. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_ip_label
The label printed before the LAN address, only when it has a value. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_wifi_label
The label printed before the Wi-Fi signal, only when it has a value. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_ssid_label
The label printed before the Wi-Fi name, only when it has a value. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_connections_label
The label printed before the connection count, only when it has a value. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_ping_label
The label printed before the latency, only when it has a value. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_public_ip_label
The label printed before the public address, only when it has a value. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_online_label
The label printed before the reachability text, only when it has a value. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_download_width
The width the download rate is padded to on the left. It wins over the fixed width, and a longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_upload_width
The width the upload rate is padded to on the left. It wins over the fixed width, and a longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_speed_width
The width both rates is padded to on the left. It wins over the fixed width, and a longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_vpn_width
The width the VPN link is padded to on the left. It wins over the fixed width, and a longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_vpn_name_width
The width the VPN name is padded to on the left. It wins over the fixed width, and a longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_ip_width
The width the LAN address is padded to on the left. It wins over the fixed width, and a longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_wifi_width
The width the Wi-Fi signal is padded to on the left. It wins over the fixed width, and a longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_ssid_width
The width the Wi-Fi name is padded to on the left. It wins over the fixed width, and a longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_connections_width
The width the connection count is padded to on the left. It wins over the fixed width, and a longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_ping_width
The width the latency is padded to on the left. It wins over the fixed width, and a longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_public_ip_width
The width the public address is padded to on the left. It wins over the fixed width, and a longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_online_width
The width the reachability text is padded to on the left. It wins over the fixed width, and a longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_medium_thresh
Download plus upload, in KB/s, that starts the medium tier. The default is 100.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_high_thresh
Download plus upload, in KB/s, that starts the high tier. The default is 1000.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_low_fg_color
The style #{net_fg_color} prints in the low tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_medium_fg_color
The style #{net_fg_color} prints in the medium tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_high_fg_color
The style #{net_fg_color} prints in the high tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_low_bg_color
The style #{net_bg_color} prints in the low tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_medium_bg_color
The style #{net_bg_color} prints in the medium tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @net_revamped_high_bg_color
The style #{net_bg_color} prints in the high tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @revamped_theme
The theme of every tmux-revamped tool, when nothing else sets one. The default
is
.BR kodougu .
.PP
The stored reading lives in
.BR @net_revamped_download ,
.BR _upload ,
.BR _total ,
the previous counters and their time, and one option per probe with its
time. apply records the placeholders the status line uses in
.BR @net_revamped_published ,
the daemon writes each one to
.BI @net_revamped_out_ name
and keeps its process id in
.BR @net_revamped_ticker_pid .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR netstat (1),
.BR ip (8),
.BR gum (1)
